{
  "case_id": "2006-05-996",
  "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 706(a) of the Bankruptcy Code provides that a debtor may convert a case under chapter 7 to a case under any other chapter of the Bankruptcy Code at any time if the case has not been converted previously from another chapter, and that any waiver of the right to convert a case under the subsection is unenforceable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David G. Baker",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The circumstances of the new case are entirely different. In fact, in that -- in the present -- the new case, the court decided that he was not eligible because his debt limit exceeded the statutory limitations that exist section 109(e). There is a three-year time span between the two, and we believe that the existing case is not moot because he still has remedies that he can obtain in Chapter 13."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But if he isn't eligible -- the new case determined that he was not eligible because his debts were too high. He didn't incur additional debts between the time of the proceeding one and proceeding two?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They're not at issue as far as this mootness question goes. I mean, you're seeking to have the right to file under 13. And if, in fact, there's no eligibility to file under 13, you're asking for the impossible. The case is simply -- you know -- it's just air."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David G. Baker",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The bankruptcy court sustained our objections to those claims and in fact reduced the total substantially."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0000-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The plain language of the statute says that, yes, Your Honor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If it has the hearing during that period, you don't dispute that the court could do that, or do you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But here there was a hearing on the motion to convert, right? There was a hearing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But your case as I understand it, your case does not turn on the question whether there was or was not, should or should not have been a hearing in this case, an evidentiary hearing in this case; is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask, I may have missed some of the colloquy here -- is it correct that he would not be eligible to file a-- to have a, institute a Chapter 13 proceeding if he had unsecured debts of over a certain amount?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: And what if at the time he makes the motion to convert, which you say he has an absolute right to make, what if the record then disclosed that he had debts exceeding that amount? What should the bankruptcy judge do in that case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is a standing Chapter 13 trustee in Chapter 13 cases that handles all the Chapter 13 cases, unless for some reason that Chapter 13 trustee must recuse him or herself. Under section 348, once the case is converted from 7 to 13, the Chapter 7 trustee services are terminated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In practical reality, that's correct, Justice Scalia. What the Chapter 13 trustee does is, if a plan is not filed, moves to dismiss the case. If a plan is filed, may look at the plan. If the plan is confirmed, acts as the disbursing agent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A bankruptcy court has the inherent authority to sanction a debtor who has acted in bad faith by denying his request to convert a Chapter 7 case to Chapter 13. Courts have the inherent authority to take appropriate action to prevent an abuse of process. Nothing in the Bankruptcy Code or section 706 purports to impair or limit the bankruptcy court's power to police the integrity of its own proceedings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0002-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Bankruptcy courts have thousands of cases, and if there is an absolute automatic right to convert, a court with thousands of cases may put off that Chapter 13 reconversion to another day."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0002-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A conversion and simultaneous conversion causes the termination and reappointment of the Chapter 7 trustee, the appointment and the immediate termination of the Chapter 13 trustee, and to the extent there's already pending Chapter 7 proceedings for dismissal or denial of discharge, the conversion would appear to us to moot those proceedings and require their reinstatement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0002-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think section 706(a) is fairly read as granting a statutory right to convert absent the two statutory exceptions or the court's proper exercise of inherent authority."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Baker",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ce955b9fad26-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Having been counsel to a Chapter 13 trustee many years ago, I can assure the Court the Chapter 13 trustees exercise all of the powers and authority that a Chapter 7 trustee does, with the exception, as was said, of possession of property of the estate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-996",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "ce955b9fad26888a2ac6e9171848b1fb0dcfbea960e87bdc253150290addb283",
      "evidence_id": "unavailable-ce955b9fad26-56",
